WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.072 --> 00:00:04.072
(bouncy, detective-style music)

00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:15.048
- [Narrator] In the
peak of summer in Italy,

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:18.068
when the beaches and lakes
are full of swimmers,

00:00:18.068 --> 00:00:20.279
the lifeguards keeping everyone safe

00:00:20.279 --> 00:00:23.362
bring in some much needed assistance.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.321
- [Narrator] Since then,
Ferruccio has found

00:00:54.321 --> 00:00:57.139
that dogs make ideal lifeguard partners.

00:00:57.139 --> 00:00:59.621
They remain calm under
pressure and instinctively

00:00:59.621 --> 00:01:01.920
choose the safest path
through the water currents

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.500
back to shore.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.489
Once in the water, they're
able to keep afloat

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:08.822
both the rescuer and the person in need.

00:01:32.594 --> 00:01:34.527
- [Narrator] To keep
up with these numbers,

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:38.150
the school has over 350
certified rescue dogs,

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:41.421
and each year, takes in new recruits.

00:01:41.421 --> 00:01:43.309
(man speaks in Italian)

00:01:43.309 --> 00:01:45.367
After about 18 months of training,

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:46.886
they learn how to jump from speeding boats

00:01:46.886 --> 00:01:51.053
and helicopters safely, among
other rescue techniques.

00:01:52.397 --> 00:01:54.243
Italy is the only country in the world

00:01:54.243 --> 00:01:56.531
that recognizes these certified canines

00:01:56.531 --> 00:01:59.256
as actual lifeguards,
but the value of this

00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:03.423
is catching on, so the school
is starting to expand abroad.

00:02:25.956 --> 00:02:30.123
(dog barking)
(bouncy, upbeat music)

00:02:31.897 --> 00:02:34.064
(chiming)

